<!-- Fold5/tablet fidelity wave 2: Android 13+ (API 33) "themed icons" -
     Material You tints every app icon on the home screen to match the
     user's wallpaper-derived palette, but only for apps that ship a
     <monochrome> layer; without one, GUIDON's icon sits as a jarring
     full-color square next to every themed icon around it once a Soldier
     turns that system setting on.

     This is the SAME guidon-flag glyph as ic_launcher_foreground.xml's
     second path (the actual icon shape), on the same 108x108 canvas so it
     aligns with the existing foreground/background layers - just without
     that file's first path (a decorative drop-shadow gradient behind the
     glyph), since Material You themed icons render as one flat tinted
     shape with no gradients to preserve. Filled solid opaque black by
     convention: the OS reads this layer's alpha only and applies its own
     dynamic color at render time, so the literal fill color here is
     inert - #FF000000 is what Android's own Image Asset tooling emits. -->
